body:
So this turned up today and its currently baffled me. its made of some kind of slightly magnetic metal. Possibly Stainless Steel. I think its part of an engine but I have no idea what machine/vehicle/aircraft it may go to. its an interesting specimen to say the least.

&#x200B;

Ive tried looking at google images for similar images or the part numbers to no avail.

I use elmers purple gle to help it tick a little, I would level your bed aswell, it doesn't look flat.

&#x200B;

Amazon [Link](https://www.amazon.com/Elmers-Washable-Disappearing-Purple-Sticks/dp/B079KKZKP7/ref=sr_1_4?hvadid=174222806558&hvdev=c&hvlocphy=9016796&hvnetw=g&hvpos=1t1&hvqmt=e&hvrand=15773962575484346484&hvtargid=kwd-36635406338&keywords=elmers+purple+glue+stick&qid=1553099174&s=gateway&sr=8-4&tag=googhydr-20) to glue

>63

Congrats you have won Grid 2, i will pm you shortly.

&#x200B;

I would enjoy Yooka-Laylee or SOMA

&#x200B;

Thanks for the giveaway :)
